  "description": "Hard-risk golden decision vector (spec section 16, PLATFORM_CONVENTIONS.md section 11; rust/risk is the reference implementation, every rule validated by unit test first, expectations filled in by rust/risk/src/bin/make_risk_golden.rs and hand-verified). The engine is built from configs/risk.json (x-version 3) with the instrument reference data below (tick_size, qty_unit = real base units per qty unit, quote_ccy), then driven through `steps` in order. Every step of type 'order' pins the expected decision (ALLOW=1 REJECT=2), the deciding rule_id (first failing rule in the pinned check order) and the RiskEvent severity (INFO=1 WARN=2 BREACH=3). Non-order steps mutate engine state: market (best bid/ask ticks at the market-data event time; a mark move can latch a loss kill with no fill), fill (position/P&L; order_id != 0 reduces that open order; a malformed fill is audited and dropped), cancel (on_order_done: the venue's terminal report — MARKET/IOC/FOK orders stay counted as open until it arrives), gap/recover (feed gate), venue_down/venue_up (connectivity), kill/unkill (manual switches), override_loss (approved loss-limit override), roll_session (daily P&L re-based). Decisions are deterministic and replayable; the audit log of a replay is byte-identical across runs AND across languages (expected_risk_audit.jsonl); the snapshot after step snapshot_after_step is expected_risk_snapshot.json and restoring it must reproduce the remaining audit tail. expected_notification_events pins the non-decision audit records (kills, latches, overrides, session roll, malformed fills, venue events), in order.",
